          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "**Emergency: Seek immediate care.** The combination of speech changes and dropping items can indicate a serious condition such as a stroke, especially if these changes are sudden. It's important to act quickly and get medical assistance.\n\nRegarding switching blood pressure tablets and drinking coffee while on medication, it's advised to discuss these concerns with your healthcare provider. Changes in medication should always be approached with professional advice. \n\nIn general, coffee consumption can affect blood pressure, as caffeine may temporarily raise blood pressure, particularly in those who do not consume it regularly. However, many individuals can safely consume moderate amounts of coffee while managing their blood pressure. It's best to consult with your clinician regarding how your specific medication interacts with caffeine and whether it's appropriate for you.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
